REMARKS:
192100Z POSITION NEAR 17.7N 84.6E.
19NOV26. TROPICAL CYCLONE 05B (AKVAN), LOCATED APPROXIMATELY 385
NM SOUTH-SOUTHWEST OF KOLKATA, INDIA, HAS TRACKED NORTH-
NORTHWESTWARD AT 08 KNOTS OVER THE PAST SIX HOURS. ANIMATED SHORTWAVE INFRARED (SWIR) SATELLITE IMAGERY DEPICTS A HIGHLY ASYMMETRIC SYSTEM, WITH AN EXPOSED LOW LEVEL CIRCULATION CENTER (LLCC) POSITIONED ON THE SOUTHWESTERN EDGE OF AN AREA OF FLARING DEEP CONVECTION. A 191445Z ASCAT-B PASS REVEALED A HIGHLY ELONGATED AND WEAK LLCC, WITH 20-25 KNOT WINDS SURROUNDING THE BULK OF THE LLCC, AND 25-30 KNOT WINDS LOCATED ALONG THE COASTLINE TO THE NORTH AND UNDER THE CONVECTION TO THE NORTHEAST. E REANALYSIS OF EARLIER ASCAT DATA SUPPORTS A DOWNGRADE OF THE SYSTEM TO A TROPICAL DEPRESSION AS EARLY AS 190600Z. NVIRONMENTAL CONDITIONS ARE GENERALLY FAVORABLE, BUT STRONGLY MITIGATED BY THE BROAD NATURE OF THE LLCC. WITH THE LIMITED TIME REMAINING OVER WATER, THE SYSTEM IS HIGHLY UNLIKELY TO HAVE ENOUGH TIME TO CONSOLIDATE OR INTENSIFY PRIOR TO LANDFALL. TC 05B WILL TRACK NORTH-NORTHWESTWARD ALONG THE WESTERN SIDE OF THE SUBTROPICAL RIDGE (STR) FAR TO THE EAST, THROUGH THE FORECAST PERIOD. LANDFALL ALONG THE EASTERN COAST OF INDIA IS EXPECTED WITHIN THE NEXT 12 HOURS, AFTER WHICH THE SYSTEM WILL CONTINUE INLAND ON A NORTHWARD TRAJECTORY. TC 05B WILL REMAIN BELOW WARNING CRITERIA THROUGH LANDFALL, AND THEN CONTINUE TO WEAKEN RAPIDLY AFTER MOVING INLAND.
THIS IS THE FINAL WARNING ON THIS SYSTEM BY THE JOINT TYPHOON
WRNCEN PEARL HARBOR HI. THE SYSTEM WILL BE CLOSELY MONITORED FOR
SIGNS OF REGENERATION. MINIMUM CENTRAL PRESSURE AT 191800Z IS
1007 MB. MAXIMUM SIGNIFICANT WAVE HEIGHT AT 191800Z IS 15 FEET.
